# fixedbugs, defect 2117, 2026-10-17, the defect's reproducer.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header defining `t3`, the name of one of the temporaries the C
# this compiler writes declares, beside a `main` of 89 chained bindings, was
# told `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at exit 2, where 88
# were told `ffi_header_refused` at exit 1: the line declaring `main`'s
# temporaries passed 4,096 bytes, clang quotes no such line, and the reader
# read the name under clang's caret in the line clang quoted.
#
# FIX: the name is read from the bytes of the line clang read, at the place a
# second clang run names without `#line`'s presumption
# (`cli/caret_bytes.hero`), and the header is refused at its line 4, exit 1.

extern "fixedbugs-2117-a-header-macro-meeting-a-temporary-on-a-line-past-4096-bytes-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function tm_f() -> i32

